Sira: Kumang, how was the ceremony?
Kumang: Boring as always. I could've spent the time searching a coconut for sepak sawut tonight.
Sira: Didn't my dad ban it for one lunar phase because a tree almost got caught on fire?
Kumang: It's been one lunar phase since then, right?
Sira: It's only been half.
Kumang: Well it is already one lunar phase to me.
Kumang: I just wanna play with Ajang again...
Sira: *sighs*
Sira: I get how you feel.
Sira: But as much as I hate my dad.
Sira: He's right. It hasn't rained in a long time.
Sira: We have to be extra cautious with lighting up fire these days. Everything burns so easily.
Sira: Why don't you play with just the coconut and no fire?
Kumang: That's boring, but alright. I understand.
Kumang: *Kumang dejectedly mulls over it while picking on the grass*
Sira: (Why hasn't it rained for a long time?)
Sira: (We have to search for a new land to plant the crops because of the drought.)